{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Do not profane your daughter to make her a harlot.</b> By giving his daughter over unwed for relations not for the purpose of kiddushin (Sanhedrin 76)." "<b>And the land shall not be harlotrous.</b> If you do so, the land makes its fruits harlotrous, producing them in another place and not in your land. And so it says ״וַיִּמָּנְעוּ רְבִיבִים״ etc. (Tosefta, Kiddushin 1)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:18.082749270Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}